PX Password Strength (visual overlay for Roundcube password plugin)
===============================================================

This plugin adds a live password strength bar and a requirements checklist
to the default Roundcube `password` plugin form in:

- Settings -> Password (`?_task=settings&_action=plugin.password`)

It is primarily a visual overlay. Server-side validation is still handled by the
Roundcube `password` plugin and its configured driver, but this plugin may also
auto-configure `password_strength_driver=px_strength` (and a default
`password_minimum_score`) when those values are not explicitly set.

Installation
------------

1. Enable plugin in `config/config.inc.php` after `password`:

   $config['plugins'] = [..., 'password', 'px_password_strength'];

2. Copy config template (optional):

   cp plugins/px_password_strength/config.inc.php.dist plugins/px_password_strength/config.inc.php

Notes
-----

- The overlay uses a local policy from `plugins/px_password_strength/config.inc.php`
  (`px_password_strength_minimum_length`, `px_password_strength_require_*`,
  `px_password_strength_forbid_diacritics`) unless shared/global override keys
  `px_password_policy_*` are set in `config/config.inc.php`.
- By default, the native `password` plugin rules list is hidden to avoid
  duplicate UI (`px_password_strength_hide_native_rules = true`).
- If `password_strength_driver` is unset (or already `px_strength`), the plugin
  sets `password_strength_driver=px_strength` and defaults
  `password_minimum_score` to `2`.
- When local `px_password_strength_minimum_length` (or shared/global
  `px_password_policy_minimum_length`) is configured, the plugin also exposes the
  effective value to the `password` plugin backend (`password_minimum_length`).
